      "body": "## Description\n\n`GatewayTrainController.update_weights()` resumed generation as soon as the\nweight exchange finished, while the new version only reached the data proxies\nlater, from `RLTrainer._update_weights_and_publish_version()`. Requests aborted\nby `pause_generation()` resubmit the moment `continue_generation()` clears the\npause state, so those segments are served by the new weights but stamped with\nthe pre-update version by `InfBridge.agenerate()` (`inf_bridge.py:227`).\n\nPer-token versions select the behavior policy used to interpolate the proximal\nlog-probabilities (`compute_prox_logp_approximations`, `actor.py:1261`), so\nmislabeled segments get the wrong off-policy correction. This is the same failure\nmode #1791 addressed for responses in flight across a version bump.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nFixes #1853\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the Contributing Guide\n- [x] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (not applicable)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [ ] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n## Additional Context\n\n`set_version()` broadcasts to every data proxy synchronously (`run_async_task`\nawaits the gather), so all proxies see the new version before any request can\nleave the pause loop. `continue_generation()` sits in a `finally` so a failed\nbroadcast cannot leave inference paused forever.\n\n`RLTrainer` still calls `rollout.set_version()` afterwards: that call is still\nneeded by the v1 controller, whose `update_weights()` neither pauses nor resumes\ngeneration, and is a no-op for v2.\n\nTests: `tests/v2/training_service` → 76 passed, 6 skipped. Both new tests fail on\nd25f292.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
